# Planning
- Know your teams tollerance & style. The past matters
  - Burned out
    - Create it yourself with one-on-one informal conversations
  - Excited
    - Create tiger teams
  - Ambivalent
    - Sell them on the why, and why you need them. 
- No plan survives contact with the real world (Field Marshal Helmuth von Moltke the Elder)

# Culture is everything
- If you build the right culture, you don't manage at all (The Culture Code)

# Leadership is omnidirectional
- Leading up is common in great organizations
  - "I don't hire smart people to tell them what to do. I hire smart people to tell me what to do."- Steve Jobs
- You will understand situations better than your boss sometimes. Lead them to a solution. Educate them. 
  - Works only with a good "boss"
  - This requires subtlety in many cases. "Flank" them. The direct approach while expedient, seldom survives your supervisor's ego.  (Jock Willink)
- Easier is to allow yourself to be lead. 
  - I like to say that "At a moment's notice, I'm a janitor."

# Prioritize and Execute (Extreme Ownership)
- Know what you are doing and why. 
- Be cautious of endeavors you have no experience in. 
- Stop, look around, make a call. Decisions are hard. Being a leader means making hard decisions regularly. 

