# Provide backup (variation on Extreme Ownership- chapter 5)
- Never assign a project without
  - A backup plan
  - A backup person
  - A schedule that allows time to bring in one or the other
  - Assessment of progress in time to do so
- For clubs, always assign a senior member and a junior member to the task.
  - If it goes well, it's a training opportunity
  - If it goes poorly, you have a backup, and a massive growth opportunity (be ready to help the junior member)

# Ensure everyone understands the mission and the parameters
- Make sure they know what to do and why well enough that they can act without you
- Provide them with training
- Provide them with courage and confidence
- The ultimate goal is to be expendable yourself
- If you are invaluable to a team as the leader, you haven't achieved success yet. 

